Task: Your task is to implement an inheritance hierarchy for musical instruments. You need to complete the `Instrument` class and then create a `StringInstrument` class that inherits from it, adding specific properties and behavior for stringed instruments.

Submitted code:
```
class Instrument {
  constructor(name) {
    // 1. Initialize the generic name property
    this.name = name;
  }

  play() {
    return `Playing the ${this.name}.`;
  }
}

// 2. StringInstrument inherits from Instrument
class StringInstrument extends Instrument {
  constructor(name, numberOfStrings) {
    // 3. Call the parent constructor to set the name
    super(name);

    // 4. Initialize specific properties
    this.numberOfStrings = numberOfStrings;
    this.type = 'String Instrument';
  }

  // 5. Implement the tune method
  tune() {
    return `Tuning the ${this.name} with ${this.numberOfStrings} strings.`;
  }
}

// --- Usage ---
const myGuitar = new StringInstrument("Guitar", 6);

console.log(myGuitar.play()); // Inherited: Playing the Guitar.
console.log(myGuitar.tune()); // Specific: Tuning the Guitar with 6 strings.
console.log(myGuitar.type); // String Instrument
```

Does this code correctly implement the inheritance concept? Check for proper OOP usage.
